{"id": "EUVD-2026-108000", "enisaUuid": "b701bc94-a2e0-3b9b-a2b0-cabadfd88e41", "description": "HAProxy 3 before 3.4.6 allows a remote unauthenticated attacker to cause a denial of service (persistent worker-thread CPU exhaustion) via an HTTP/1.1 chunked request. Although the H1 multiplexer drains the request before closing the stream, the parser repeatedly re-processes the same bytes without making progress. The affected thread stays busy at 100% CPU after timeouts expire and after the client disconnects, and repeated requests can consume all worker threads until the process is restarted.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T02:46:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:10:34", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.haproxy.org/?p=haproxy.git;a=commit;h=077906da140a35873bf451d7e9f67646c9f37c81"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vqpp-w68q-p3f5", "CVE-2026-110354"], "assigner": "mitre", "epss": 0.76, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1ad91c57-a256-320d-8893-bfef168c8ab0", "product": {"name": "HAProxy Enterprise Edition", "vendor": {"name": "HAProxy"}}, "product_version": "3.0r1 <3.0r1-362.1441"}, {"id": "2cc3be7b-8f5f-3946-b965-adf41681ed3e", "product": {"name": "Kubernetes Ingress Controller Enterprise", "vendor": {"name": "HAProxy Technologies"}}, "product_version": "3.2.0 <3.2.17-ee1"}, {"id": "35b5274c-b1e1-3895-965d-133f00592737", "product": {"name": "Kubernetes Ingress Controller Enterprise", "vendor": {"name": "HAProxy Technologies"}}, "product_version": "3.0 <3.0.16-ee17"}, {"id": "5c32d771-e917-39be-8399-0780286c7429", "product": {"name": "HAProxy Enterprise Edition", "vendor": {"name": "HAProxy"}}, "product_version": "3.2r1 <3.2r1-378.1259"}, {"id": "630495da-6bae-353b-b76f-0a37dd3f959b", "product": {"name": "haproxy", "vendor": {"name": "HAProxy"}}, "product_version": "3.3.0 <3.3.17"}, {"id": "70fd888c-5bcf-3049-895f-4d79a0b826c6", "product": {"name": "HAProxy Enterprise Edition", "vendor